# One-off backtest reports (scripts/tune_xg_weight.py, tune_sos_strength.py,
# tune_rest_days.py, tune_motivation.py, tune_referee.py, tune_weather.py) -
# not read by anything live; a finding worth shipping gets hardcoded into
# goals_model.py/xg_blend.py (or similar) by hand instead.
data/xg-weights.json
data/sos-strengths.json
data/rest-days-strengths.json
data/motivation-strengths.json
data/referee-strengths.json
data/weather-strengths.json

# Local dev cache for scripts/euro_fixtures.py (historical UEFA fixture
# lookups for tune_rest_days.py) and scripts/weather_data.py (Meteostat
# station data, tune_weather.py) - backtest-only, not part of the live
# pipeline, safe to re-fetch if lost.
data/cache/espn_euro/
data/cache/meteostat/

# NOTE: data/cache/wikidata_stadiums/ is NOT ignored - scripts/stadium_geo.py's
# club_qid() cache is reused live by scripts/fetch_injuries.py every hourly
# run (Wikidata club id -> Transfermarkt team id), so it's committed like
# data/cache/openfootball to avoid re-resolving every club from scratch
# each run (slow, and Wikidata's public endpoints throttle hard - see that
# module's docstring).

# Legacy Streamlit path (not used by the static app)
predictions.xlsx
*.xlsx
